| `make canary` `[read]` | Renders each configured answer set fresh and as an update from the previous release tag, and runs that project's own `make verify`, so a release cannot ship a template whose projects fail their own gate. | `make canary`, or one set on the farm: `make canary CANARY_FLAGS="--set skeleton"` | [`canary.answer_sets`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`canary.scratch_root`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`CANARY_FLAGS`](settings.md#make-variables) | Runs from the template checkout only; in a generated project it names that checkout and exits 2. Not part of `make verify`: one run is a project verify per set and path, so the farm, the weekly workflow and the release step run it. [read]: npm and the browser download reach the network. | [CONTRIBUTING.md](../../CONTRIBUTING.md) | always |
